        "Describe cortisol's effects on mood and memory, including how chronic exposure can impair the very brain regions that regulate the stress response.",
        "Distinguish training as a deliberately chosen stressor from uncontrolled life stress, and explain how the same cortisol response can drive adaptation in one case and contribute to overtraining in the other.",
        "Recognize adrenal fatigue and cortisol detox claims as unsupported by evidence, and grade the quality of common stress-management approaches.",
        "Apply evidence-based stress management strategies to daily life, and know exactly where general education about cortisol ends and a qualified clinician's diagnosis of a genuine cortisol disorder, such as Cushing's syndrome or Addison's disease, begins."
